Every vendored file = an 8-line provenance banner + the byte-identical
upstream body. sha256 below covers the PRISTINE body (strip the banner:
first 8 lines). All files MUST come from the same tag -- utils/readable/
writable/destroy share the kState bitfield layout; mixed-tag vendoring
silently corrupts it (docs/design/streams-port.md section 2).

Deliberately not vendored: lazy_transform.js (crypto extends Transform
directly), stream/consumers.js (oam keeps its own), stream/web.js +
internal/webstreams/adapters (bridged to js/streams.js; stub in slice 2),
internal/streams/iter/* (v26 readable.js requires classic.js + types.js
lazily, only behind getOptionValue('--experimental-stream-iter'), which
oam's internal/options shim answers false -- oam has no stream/iter).

Also vendored, though not a streams file: internal/fixed_queue.js (v26
readable.js's async iterator queues through it). It moves with the rest.

Gate: crates/oam_engine/tests/vendored_streams_upstream.rs re-hashes every
body below against this table (cargo test -p oam_engine), so a file edited
in place, a stale row, a banner naming another tag, or an unlisted file
fails the build's tests. Offline it cannot see a body left behind with its
banner re-stamped and its row untouched (the v22.23.5 readable.js miss);
its #[ignore]d network test fetches every row at COMMIT and compares:
  cargo test -p oam_engine --test vendored_streams_upstream -- --ignored

Re-vendor procedure (Node version bump):
  1. Update TAG + COMMIT here (deref the annotated tag via the GitHub API).
  2. For each file below: fetch source-base/<path>, verify sha256 of the
     fetched body changes ONLY when upstream changed, re-prepend the banner
     (update tag/commit/date), write, and update the table row.
  3. Re-derive the primordials union + shim surface (slice-2 extraction
     script) BEFORE running the suite -- new upstream code may widen it.
  4. Run the gate WITH its network test (command above): every row must
     match the pinned commit.
  5. cargo run -p xtask -- node-suite && conformance; full ci-local before
     commit. All files move together or not at all.

